# Touch A's Goodix driver reports abs_max=4095 but only uses ~0..800 for X
# and ~0..1280 for Y (panel pixel coords) in the panel's native portrait.
#
# The panel runs native portrait, but Xorg presents the menu rotated "left"
# (landscape). The touch therefore needs a matching 90 CW rotation folded into
# the calibration on top of the active-area scaling — without it the cursor
# tracks 90 off (drag right -> cursor up, drag down -> cursor right, etc).
#
# Matrix below is R(90 CW) . scaling, as a 2x3 LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX:
#   scaling : x*5.120 (=4095/800), y*3.199 (=4095/1280) -> active area fills [0,1]
#   rotated : (u,v) -> (1 - 3.199*v, 5.120*u)
ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}=="1", ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="0 -3.199 1 5.120 0 0"
